Mental model (very important)

List comprehension → “Compute everything now” stores in memeory all elemnets

Generator → “Compute only when asked”, genertaes each element lazily , gets exhausted after 1 iteration, can not
be reused unless recreated
Why row count increases after merge
What you said

Missing on clause → Cartesian product

outer join instead of inner

✔️ First point is valid
❌ Second point is NOT the main reason for row explosion

An outer join can increase rows slightly, but it usually does not explode rows.

The REAL two interview-grade reasons
✅ Reason 1: Many-to-many join

This is the most common cause.

Example:

Left table: User A appears 3 times

Right table: User A appears 2 times

After merge → 3 × 2 = 6 rows for User A

This happens when the join key is not unique in either table.

✅ Reason 2: Wrong or missing join key

Missing on clause → Cartesian product

Or joining on the wrong column (non-unique key)

This causes combinatorial row growth.

“The most common reason for an unexpected increase in rows after a merge is 
a many-to-many join, where the join key is not unique in one or both DataFrames. 
Another reason is using the wrong or missing join key, which can result in a Cartesian product. 
Join type like outer vs inner
affects row inclusion but is usually not the main cause of row explosion.”

“Before merging, I usually check key
uniqueness using value_counts() or duplicated() to avoid unintended many-to-many joins.”

